<title>JAPAN: Mikuni assigns preliminary bond credit ratings.</title>
<headline>Mikuni assigns preliminary bond credit ratings.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-04-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mikuni and Co Ltd said on Friday it had assigned the following preliminary ratings to planned bond issues:</p>
<p>-AA-</p>
<p>Chubu Electric Power Co Inc, 50 billion yen mortgaged due 2017</p>
<p>Hokuriku Electric Power Co Inc., 30 billion yen mortgaged due 2017</p>
<p>Kokusai Denshin Denwa Co Ltd.,</p>
<p>20 billion yen mortgaged due 2009</p>
<p>20 billion yen mortgaged due 2017  </p>
<p>-A-</p>
<p>Saibu Gas Co Ltd., 20 billion yen unsecured due 2004</p>
<p>-BB-</p>
<p>The Maruetsu Inc, 10 billion yen unsecured due 2004</p>
<p>Nippon Felt Co Ltd, three billion yen unsecured convertible due 2004</p>
<p>Sanko Gosei Ltd, two billion yen unsecured convertible due 2001, private placement  </p>
<p>-B-</p>
<p>Tobu Railway Co Ltd,</p>
<p>10 billion yen unsecured due 2003</p>
<p>10 billion yen unsecured due 2009</p>
<p>10 billion yen unsecured due 2012</p>
</text>
